"KTPH000","f":["<img alt=\"Main window layout\" src=\"../assets/diagrams/mainwindow-layout.svg\" />"]},{"s":32970,"e":33162,"k":"block","t":"A fresh korTTY window: the menu bar, the terminal area (where session tabs and the optional dashboard appear once you connect), and the status bar. The following diagram maps the same regions:","f":[]},{"s":33170,"e":33245,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000","f":["<img alt=\"korTTY architecture\" src=\"../assets/diagrams/architecture.svg\" />"]},{"s":33253,"e":33292,"k":"block","t":"korTTY's main window has these regions:","f":[]},{"s":33306,"e":33657,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Menu barKTPH001 — File · Edit · Connections · Security · Configuration · Tools · Plugins · View · Teamwork · AI · Help. All features are reachable here and via KTPH002keyboard shortcutsKTPH003. A live KTPH004JobScheduler statusKTPH005 menu appears after KTPH006HelpKTPH007 when a scheduled entry is active.","f":["<strong>","</strong>","<a href=\"../reference/keyboard-shortcuts.html\">","</a>","<strong>","</strong>","<em>","</em>"]},{"s":33667,"e":34433,"k":"block","t":"KTPH007Tab barKTPH008 — each SSH/Mosh session runs in its own tab. KTPH009KTPH000KTPH010+KTPH011KTPH001KTPH012 opens Quick Connect for a new tab; KTPH013KTPH002KTPH014+KTPH015KTPH003KTPH016 / KTPH017KTPH004KTPH018+KTPH019KTPH005KTPH020+KTPH021KTPH006KTPH022 switch tabs. With KTPH023Open tool windows as tabsKTPH024 enabled (KTPH025Window settingsKTPH026), management tools such as Snippets, the JobScheduler or the AI Manager open here as tabs too — in the window whose menu you used — instead of as separate windows.","f":["<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-t\">T</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-tab\">Tab</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-shift\">Shift</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-tab\">Tab</kbd>","<strong>","</strong>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","</span>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","</span>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","<span>","</span>","</span>","<strong>","</strong>","<a href=\"../reference/settings/window.html\">","</a>"]},{"s":34443,"e":34774,"k":"block","t":"KTPH003DashboardKTPH004 (toggle KTPH005KTPH000KTPH006+KTPH007KTPH001KTPH008+KTPH009KTPH002KTPH010) — a side panel listing every open connection with status dots, protocol badges and AI-agent badges. See KTPH011DashboardKTPH012 below.","f":["<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-shift\">Shift</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-d\">D</kbd>","<strong>","</strong>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","<span>","</span>","</span>","<a href=\"#dashboard\">","</a>"]},{"s":34784,"e":35155,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000File browserKTPH001 (KTPH002View → File Browser ▸ Show on Left / Show on RightKTPH003) — a dockable local file manager with navigation toolbar, path bar, filter, type icons and a folder/file/selection counter. Its side, width, hidden-file state and last directory are restored on the next launch. See KTPH004File browserKTPH005.","f":["<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>","<a href=\"../features/file-browser.html\">","</a>"]},{"s":35165,"e":35266,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Terminal areaKTPH001 — the active terminal, with optional split-screen and broadcast input.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":35276,"e":35398,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Status barKTPH001 — connection state, host/IP, active protocol, temporary SSH-key timer and connection duration.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":35467,"e":35491,"k":"block","t":"Terminal-only fullscreen","f":[]},{"s":35499,"e":36312,"k":"block","t":"Press KTPH006KTPH000KTPH007+KTPH008KTPH001KTPH009+KTPH010KTPH002KTPH011 (or KTPH012View → Terminal-only FullscreenKTPH013) to show the whole korTTY window — menus, tabs and status bar included — kept at its previous window size and centered on an empty fullscreen background, so the desktop and other windows stop competing for attention. KTPH014View → Hide terminal scrollbars in fullscreenKTPH015 removes the scrollbars too. A transparent terminal background becomes opaque while fullscreen is active and returns to its saved level when you leave. Press KTPH016KTPH003KTPH017+KTPH018KTPH004KTPH019+KTPH020KTPH005KTPH021 again to restore.","f":["<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-shift\">Shift</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-f\">F</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-shift\">Shift</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-f\">F</kbd>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","<span>","</span>","</span>","<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","<span>","</span>","</span>"]},{"s":36343,"e":36425,"k":"block","t":"DashboardKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#dashboard\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":36434,"e":36760,"k":"block","t":"Toggle the dashboard with KTPH003KTPH000KTPH004+KTPH005KTPH001KTPH006+KTPH007KTPH002KTPH008 or KTPH009View → Show DashboardKTPH010. It slides in on the left, sizes its width to the longest entry, and follows the active App Design's colors.","f":["<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-shift\">Shift</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-d\">D</kbd>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","<span>","</span>","</span>","<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":36768,"e":36988,"k":"block","t":"The header shows the panel title with two buttons: a collapse/expand toggle (collapses everything while any node is open, expands everything otherwise) and a refresh button. Below it, connections are organized as a tree:","f":[]},{"s":37002,"e":37083,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Main windowKTPH001 — the root node, with an active/total session count.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":37093,"e":37331,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000EnvironmentsKTPH001 — connections whose stored credential has an environment (for example KTPH002ProductionKTPH003 or KTPH004TestKTPH005) are clustered under an environment node; connections without one sit directly under the main window.","f":["<strong>","</strong>","<em>","</em>","<em>","</em>"]},{"s":37341,"e":37513,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000GroupsKTPH001 — tabs assigned to a connection group appear under their group node. Saving a changed group in the Connection Manager updates open tabs immediately.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":37528,"e":38160,"k":"block","t":"Each connection row shows a type icon, a status dot, the server name, and a protocol badge (KTPH000, KTPH001 or KTPH002). The status dot distinguishes three states: filled green for a healthy connection, filled red for a connection that dropped unexpectedly (including a Mosh network interruption), and a hollow outline for a session that ended normally. Terminals with AI-agent runs carry the same ✋/⚡/⏸/✓ badge as elsewhere. Hovering a row shows KTPH003 and the connection state; double-click (or KTPH005KTPH004KTPH006) focuses the session's tab.","f":["<code>ssh</code>","<code>mosh</code>","<code>local</code>","<code>user@host</code>","<kbd class=\"key-enter\">Enter</kbd>","<span class=\"keys\">","</span>"]},{"s":38168,"e":38485,"k":"block","t":"Right-click a connection for KTPH000FocusKTPH001, KTPH002DuplicateKTPH003, KTPH004ReconnectKTPH005, KTPH006SFTP-Client...KTPH007 (connected sessions only) and KTPH008CloseKTPH009. A footer keeps a running \"connected of total\" count, and an empty panel shows a placeholder until the first session opens.","f":["<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":38515,"e":38609,"k":"block","t":"macOS Dock menuKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#macos-dock-menu\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":38618,"e":38814,"k":"block","t":"On macOS, right-click (or Control-click) the korTTY icon in the Dock for quick actions without switching to the app — they apply to the current (focused) window, opening one first if none is open:","f":[]},{"s":38828,"e":38855,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000New WindowKTPH001","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":38865,"e":38907,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000New Tab in Current WindowKTPH001","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":38917,"e":38974,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Manage Connections…KTPH001 (Connection Manager)","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":38984,"e":39014,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Open Project…KTPH001","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":39024,"e":39066,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000ManualKTPH001 (the in-app guide)","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":39076,"e":39105,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000About korTTYKTPH001","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":39120,"e":39322,"k":"block","t":"See the KTPH000menu referenceKTPH001 for every menu item and the KTPH002keyboard-shortcuts referenceKTPH003 for the full list of accelerators.","f":["<a href=\"../reference/menu.html\">","</a>","<a href=\"../reference/keyboard-shortcuts.html\">","</a>"]},{"s":40193,"e":40208,"k":"text","t":"\n  Back to top\n","f":[]},{"s":40451,"e":40492,"k":"text","t":"MIT-licensed · Developed by Daniel Mengel","f":[]},{"s":40538,"e":40550,"k":"text","t":"\n    korTTY ","f":[]},{"s":40558,"e":40564,"k":"text","t":"v2.7.0","f":[]}]}